// `j3c -e scene` / `render`: scene edits and checks by object name.
//
// Port of: j3c/src/scene/mod.rs
// J3: In-process (plan 11 B12.1): uses `j3c/editor/src/tool.j3` (and `tool/` parts) and `j3.scene3d`
// directly. No editor build, no spawn per call, no per-version editor cache for headless ops. `render`
// needs GL and may stay an offscreen-SDL subprocess; decide in C5 and write the choice here. With an
// editor open, edits go through `j3.instance` `request` to its `App.onRequest` (B12.2; `live.j3` becomes
// that handler). Tool args and help come from the one tool table in `mcp/schema` (B12.3).
module j3c.scene;
